(Network Hardening Best Practices \(Reference for RAG\)) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(1. Segmentation and Least Privilege) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Separate user, management, and service planes.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Permit only required east-west and north-south flows.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Apply deny-by-default in forwarding policy.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(2. Router/Switch Control Plane Protection) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Disable unnecessary services \(for example telnet\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Restrict management protocols to trusted sources.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Drop invalid conntrack state packets.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(3. Baseline Kernel/Network Stack Hardening) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Disable ICMP redirects handling where unnecessary.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Disable sending redirects from routers.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Ignore broadcast ICMP echo requests.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(4. Monitoring and Verification) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Verify policy outcomes with active probes \(ping/tcp tests\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Collect change records and implementation timestamps.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Confirm both intended connectivity and intended blocks.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(5. Secure Change Management) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Make changes idempotent \(safe to re-apply\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Store exact command/action logs for each request.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Provide explicit success/failure confirmation.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(6. Common Immediate Controls) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Block plaintext protocols \(telnet, legacy cleartext mgmt\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Limit ICMP where abuse is a concern, preserving diagnostics.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Enforce source/destination based forwarding filters.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(7. Operational Notes) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Test in emulated topologies before production rollout.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Keep an emergency rollback path for policy changes.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Reassess hardening controls after topology changes.) Tj
ET
